<title>INDIA: India soybean steady, soymeal, extractions firm.</title>
<headline>India soybean steady, soymeal, extractions firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Daily arrivals fell to around 1,000 tonnes in the central Indian markets of central India from around 15,000 tonnes during the same period last year, traders said.</p>
<p>Soyoil was steady on a better note, but volumes were low.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction were firm on enquiries from the international market, traders said. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $306-307 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $117 per tonne FAS in bulk for export. Rapeseed was 4,050 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Offerings from Indian processors and exporters were limited.</p>
